# DESCRIPTION
# A simple grade 4 fraction word problem.
# ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Arithmetic')
## DBchapter('Fractions')
## DBsection('Word problems')
## KEYWORDS('word problem', 'fraction', 'money')
## Author('Peter Staab')
## Institution('Fitchburg State University')
## Date('04/05/2021')

#updated 2023.03.17

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',   'PGML.pl',
    'randomPerson.pl', 'contextFraction.pl',
    'PGcourse.pl'
);

# make sure we're in the context we want
Context("Fraction");

do {
    $x = random(3, 5);
    $y = random(3, 5);
} until ($x != $y);

$prod = $x * $y;
$left = $prod - $x;

$p = randomPerson();

$f   = Compute("$x/$prod");
$ans = Compute("1-$f")->reduce;

BEGIN_PGML

[$p] has $[`[$prod]`].  [$p->They] [$p->verb('buy')] a toy for $[`[$x]`].  What fraction of [$p->their] money [$p->do] [$p->they] have left?

[________]{$ans}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

The are two ways to do this.

*Method 1*

The fraction of the money spent is [`\frac{[$x]}{[$prod]}`] which reduces to [`[$f]`].

The fraction that she has left is [`1-[$f]=[$ans]`]

*Method 2*

The amount of money that is left is [`[$prod]-[$x]=[$left]`].

The fraction left then is [`\frac{[$left]}{[$prod]}`] which reduces to [`[$ans]`].
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
